==============================================================================================================
VERDICT (W1-W4)
==============================================================================================================
  A swirled river pushes co-moving (prograde) and counter-moving (retrograde) bodies oppositely: that sign flip is the
  swirl's fingerprint.  GR's own swirl of the Milky Way's river (frame dragging) is about a millionth of Newtonian gravity
  at the Sun's radius: the river turns at ~a metre per second; no galactic observable can see it.

